        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the derivative term is already isolated on the left:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x) &=8 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides of the equation with respect to $x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int f\\prime(x)\\,\\text{d}x &=\\int (8 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(x) &=\\int (8 x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ &=1\\cdot \\left(4 x^{2}\\right)+C \\\\ &=4 x^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
